        "original_id": "dd6bb349-273d-5306-a16b-0e302857b294",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Canals: Sandy and Beaver Canal; Beaver and Erie Canal\n- Places: Bolivar, Ohio; Glasgow, Pennsylvania; Ohio River; Lake Erie; Beaver County; Lawrence County; Mercer County; Crawford County; Erie County; Pennsylvania; Ohio\n- Systems: Ohio and Erie Canal; Pennsylvania Canal system\n- Concepts: canal divisions\n\nFacts:\n- The Sandy and Beaver Canal ran 73 miles from the Ohio and Erie Canal at Bolivar, Ohio, to the Ohio River at Glasgow, Pennsylvania.\n- The Beaver and Erie Canal was also known as the Erie Extension Canal.\n- The Beaver and Erie Canal was part of the Pennsylvania Canal system.\n- The Beaver and Erie Canal consisted of the Beaver Division, the Shenango Division, and the Conneaut Division.\n- The Beaver and Erie Canal ran 136 miles north to south near the western edge of Pennsylvania from the Ohio River to Lake Erie through Beaver County, Lawrence County, Mercer County, Crawford County, and Erie County.",
